<p>An 85-year-old French woman, Marie-Thérèse Ross, has returned to France after US Immigration and Customs Enforcement detained her in Alabama on April 1 for overstaying her visa. French officials later confirmed her return, bringing a calmer end to a case that drew attention because of her age, her recent bereavement, and the circumstances that brought her to the United States. Ross moved to the US after reconnecting with an American man she had known decades earlier, but he died in January, according to the reports. ICE said she had stayed beyond the 90-day period allowed under her visa status, while NDTV reported that her detention unfolded amid a dispute involving her late husband&#x27;s family and estate.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/MOSGokP2vB0smo56fykfgVZSxpx-9Baotv7p75S1rlIuw19VyDTB8gB4lBrHXZOcWRIF1zhLjCJOYnD297TMn4NjhdpFBBqAFjYDtwDvDYvBOprhvf7cXg-c8wHYtwqd_6FLTV9Nx0tBPp71ZVY' alt='Image accompanying reports on Marie-Thérèse Ross&#x27;s return to France after US immigration detention.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Diplomatic timing: France publicly called for Ross&#x27;s release on Thursday, and AllSides said ICE released her on Friday before she returned home.</li><li>Detention site: After ICE arrested her in Alabama, authorities held Ross at a federal detention center in Louisiana before she left the United States.</li><li>Family fallout: NDTV said Ross&#x27;s stepson stepped in after his father&#x27;s death amid a dispute over the estate.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>French government: France treated the case as an urgent consular matter and publicly pressed for Ross&#x27;s release because of her age. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/85-year-old-widow-detained-by-ice-returns-home-frances-foreign-minister-says'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>ICE: US immigration authorities described the detention as an immigration enforcement action tied to an alleged visa overstay. (<a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-04-17-0700/immigration-french-widow-us-veteran-returns-france-after-ice-detention'>AllSides</a>)</li><li>Ross&#x27;s family: Her daughter described the family&#x27;s emotional strain and welcomed Ross&#x27;s return to France. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/ce84j0j6622o'>BBC News</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/ce84j0j6622o'>&#x27;Mum is finally free!&#x27; Pensioner detained by ICE in US returns to France</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/85-year-old-widow-detained-by-ice-returns-home-frances-foreign-minister-says'>85-year-old widow detained by ICE returns home, France&#x27;s foreign minister says</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/marie-therese-ross-french-widow-85-returns-home-after-being-detained-in-us-amid-family-fight-11374443#publisher=newsstand'>French Widow, 85, Returns Home After Being Detained In US Amid Family Fight</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-04-17-0700/immigration-french-widow-us-veteran-returns-france-after-ice-detention'>French widow of US veteran returns to France after ICE detention</a> - allsides.com</li></ul>